        "title": "or absolute, starting with a slash:\\",
        "section": "Automatically “sniffing” the delimiter \\",
        "text": "\\\n`read_csv` is capable of inferring delimited (not necessarily\\\ncomma-separated) files, as pandas uses the `csv.Sniffer`\\\nclass of the csv module. For this, you have to specify `sep=None`.\\\n\\\n```\\\nIn [221]: df = pd.DataFrame(np.random.randn(10, 4))\\\n\\\nIn [222]: df.to_csv(\"tmp2.csv\", sep=\":\", index=False)\\\n\\\nIn [223]: pd.read_csv(\"tmp2.csv\", sep=None, engine=\"python\")\\\nOut[223]:\\\n          0         1         2         3\\\n0  0.469112 -0.282863 -1.509059 -1.135632\\\n1  1.212112 -0.173215  0.119209 -1.044236\\\n2 -0.861849 -2.104569 -0.494929  1.071804\\\n3  0.721555 -0.706771 -1.039575  0.271860\\\n4 -0.424972  0.567020  0.276232 -1.087401\\\n5 -0.673690  0.113648 -1.478427  0.524988\\\n6  0.404705  0.577046 -1.715002 -1.039268\\\n7 -0.370647 -1.157892 -1.344312  0.844885\\\n8  1.075770 -0.109050  1.643563 -1.469388\\\n9  0.357021 -0.674600 -1.776904 -0.968914\\\n```\\\n\\\nCopy to clipboard\\\n\\",
